To create a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image, you can use the Gutenberg Block API. Here's a step-by-step guide to help you create a custom block:

1. First, make sure you have Node.js and npm installed on your computer. If not, you can download and install them from https://nodejs.org/

2. Create a new directory for your block and navigate to it in your terminal:

```
mkdir my-custom-block
cd my-custom-block
```

3. Initialize a new npm project and install the necessary dependencies:

```
npm init -y
npm install @wordpress/blocks @wordpress/i18n @wordpress/element @wordpress/components
```

4. Create a new file called `index.js` in the root of your block directory and paste the following code:

```javascript
import { registerBlockType } from '@wordpress/blocks';
import { RichText, MediaUpload, BlockControls } from '@wordpress/editor';
import { Button } from '@wordpress/components';

registerBlockType('my-plugin/my-custom-block', {
    title: 'My Custom Block',
    icon: 'smiley',
    category: 'common',
    attributes: {
        title: {
            type: 'string',
            source: 'html',
            selector: 'h2',
        },
        content: {
            type: 'string',
            source: 'html',
            selector: 'p',
        },
        imageAlt: {
            attribute: 'alt',
            selector: '.my-image',
        },
        imageUrl: {
            attribute: 'src',
            selector: '.my-image',
        },
    },
    edit({ attributes, setAttributes }) {
        const { title, content, imageAlt, imageUrl } = attributes;

        const onChangeTitle = (newTitle) => {
            setAttributes({ title: newTitle });
        };

        const onChangeContent = (newContent) => {
            setAttributes({ content: newContent });
        };

        const onMediaUpload = (media) => {
            setAttributes({ imageUrl: media.url, imageAlt: media.alt });
        };

        const onRemoveImage = () => {
            setAttributes({ imageUrl: '', imageAlt: '' });
        };

        return (
            <div className="my-custom-block">
                <BlockControls>
                    <MediaUpload
                        onSelect={onMediaUpload}
                        type="image"
                        value={imageUrl}
                        render={({ open }) => (
                            <Button onClick={open} isSecondary={true}>
                                Add Image
                            </Button>
                        )}
                    />
                    {imageUrl && (
                        <Button isSecondary={true} onClick={onRemoveImage}>
                            Remove Image
                        </Button>
                    )}
                </BlockControls>
                <RichText
                    tagName="h2"
                    value={title}
                    onChange={onChangeTitle}
                    placeholder="Your Heading"
                />
                <RichText
                    tagName="p"
                    value={content}
                    onChange={onChangeContent}
                    placeholder="Your Content"
                />
                <div className="my-image">
                    {imageUrl && <img src={imageUrl} alt={imageAlt} />}
                </div>
            </div>
        );
    },
    save({ attributes }) {
        const { title, content, imageAlt, imageUrl } = attributes;

        return (
            <div className="my-custom-block">
                {imageUrl && <img src={imageUrl} alt={imageAlt} />}
                <h2>{title}</h2>
                <p>{content}</p>
            </div>
        );
    },
});
```

